  "Finished in 1909 as the LaGrange Township Library, with $10,000 from Carnegie; the county library ran from its basement from 1947 to 1957. The township library closed in 1993, and the building reopened in October 1994 as the Cass District Library's local history branch; it was renovated in 2020–21.",
